module absorbanceDetection
module lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection
module rosFluorescenceDetection

manifest CyclotellaCryptica
manifest LipidTOX_Stock
manifest DCFDA_Kit
manifest AscorbicAcid
manifest FC_Medium
manifest FC_Medium_NoSilicon
manifest LED_BlueArray
manifest LED_YellowArray

// ============================================================
// A Droplet-Based Screen for Wavelength-Dependent Lipid
// Production in Algae.
// Shih, Mufti, Chamberlain, Kim, Wheeler
// Energy Environ. Sci., 2014, DOI: 10.1039/c4ee01123f
//
// Protocol: Digital microfluidic (DMF) long-term culture and
// multiplexed screening of Cyclotella cryptica for neutral
// lipid production under varying LED illumination wavelengths
// (multicolour screen then blue/yellow cycling screen), plus
// a reactive oxygen species (ROS) mechanistic assay.
//
// DEVICE OVERVIEW:
//   Two four-electrode active reservoirs (algae + LipidTOX),
//   8 bussed dye-dispensing electrodes, 8 algae culture zone
//   electrodes, 8 absorbance detection electrodes (L-shaped),
//   8 fluorescence detection electrodes, 8 waste reservoir
//   electrodes with 1 mm through-holes. Detection pitch: 9 mm,
//   compatible with standard 384-well multiwell plate reader.
//   Narrow dispenser electrodes (>=0.5:1 ratio to destination)
//   ensure reliable parallel dispensing on bussed electrodes.
//
// ALGAE CULTURE CONDITIONS:
//   C. cryptica (CCMP 332) in f/2 medium + biotin +
//   cyanocobalamin + 0.02% w/v Pluronic F68, 20 C,
//   12 h white light / 12 h dark alternating cycle.
//   Inoculation density: ~9.0e5 cells/mL (exponential phase).
//   Cell suspension: 1.5e6 cells/mL in complete media.
//   LipidTOX working solution: stock diluted 200x in media.
//
// SCREENING DESIGN:
//   PROTOCOL 1 (multicolour): 7 LED wavelengths (red, orange,
//     yellow, green, blue, purple, white) + dark control, at
//     low (50 umol/m2/s) and high (250 umol/m2/s) intensity,
//     all LEDs on for 24 h. This .bs file encodes the HIGH
//     intensity arm as the representative protocol (Fig. 3b,d,f).
//     A separate run is needed for low intensity (Fig. 3a,c,e).
//   PROTOCOL 2 (blue/yellow cycling): 8 timed blue/yellow
//     combinations at high intensity (250 umol/m2/s). Only the
//     optimal condition (15 h blue / 9 h yellow) is encoded here
//     as the representative arm (Fig. 4a,b). Other timing
//     variants follow identical structure with different heat
//     durations.
//   PROTOCOL 3 (ROS mechanistic assay): DCFDA fluorescence
//     to quantify reactive oxygen species under yellow vs. blue
//     vs. normal conditions, and with ascorbate antioxidant
//     (Fig. 5c). Encoded as a sequential three-condition assay.
//
// DETECTION:
//   Absorbance at 660 nm (cell density proxy), PHERAstar reader,
//   scan matrix 15x15, scan width 3 mm, focal height 8.7 mm.
//   Fluorescence: 488 nm excitation / 520 nm emission (LipidTOX),
//   scan matrix 20x20, scan width 3 mm, focal height 8.7 mm,
//   gain = 550. DCFDA: excitation 490 nm / emission 526 nm.
//
// KEY FINDINGS ENCODED:
//   Yellow LEDs (580 nm) cause >2x neutral lipid accumulation
//   vs. control; 15 h blue / 9 h yellow cycling produces ~4x
//   lipid increase (best hit). Yellow light correlates with
//   elevated ROS; ascorbate reverses the effect, consistent
//   with photooxidative stress mechanism.
//
// NOTE ON TIMING ABSTRACTION:
//   BioScript `heat` durations use s/m tokens only.
//   6 h = 360m, 9 h = 540m, 15 h = 900m, 18 h = 1080m,
//   24 h = 1440m. All conversions applied below.
//
// NOTE ON PARALLELISM ABSTRACTION:
//   The DMF device simultaneously cultures 8 droplets per
//   condition. BioScript encodes a single representative
//   droplet lineage per condition. The bussed electrode
//   architecture handles parallelism in hardware. Three
//   physical device replicates (n=3) are run separately.
//
// NOTE ON ACTIVE RESERVOIR:
//   Both reservoirs (algae suspension and LipidTOX) are
//   continuously circulated on their four active electrodes
//   to maintain homogeneous cell density before each
//   dispense step. This is abstracted as a `mix` loop on
//   the reservoir droplets prior to culture dispensing.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- device loading, active reservoir
//                             mixing, multicolour screen (P1)
//   BB2  colourPass        -- absorbSignal1 > 0: valid cell
//                             density; proceed to fluorescence
//   BB3  colourFail        -- absorbSignal1 <= 0: no cells; drain
//   BB4  colourJoin        -- join: blue/yellow screen (P2)
//   BB5  blueYellowPass    -- absorbSignal2 > 0: proceed to ROS
//   BB6  blueYellowFail    -- absorbSignal2 <= 0: drain
//   BB7  blueYellowJoin    -- join: ROS mechanistic assay (P3)
//   BB8  rosYellowPass     -- rosSignalYellow > 0: valid ROS
//                             signal; dispose
//   BB9  rosYellowFail     -- rosSignalYellow <= 0: drain
//   BB10 finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// DEVICE LOADING (STEP 1):
// Load algae suspension (150 uL, 1.5e6 cells/mL) and LipidTOX
// working solution (120 uL, 200x diluted stock) into their
// respective active reservoirs. Each reservoir circulates
// continuously on four electrodes to prevent cell settling
// and maintain homogeneous density before dispensing.
// These are the only two manual pipette steps required for
// a full 24 h run generating 48 measurements.
// NOTE: `mix` abstracts active-reservoir continuous circulation
// (not a single mixing event); duration = pre-dispense hold.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

algaeReservoir     = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica
lipidTOXReservoir  = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock

// Active reservoir circulation to maintain cell homogeneity
// before culture droplets are dispensed (Step 2).
algaeCirculating   = mix algaeReservoir with algaeReservoir for 10s
lipidTOXCirculating = mix lipidTOXReservoir with lipidTOXReservoir for 10s

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 1: MULTICOLOUR LED SCREEN (HIGH INTENSITY)
// 7 wavelength conditions + dark control, 250 umol/m2/s,
// all LEDs on for 24 h. Encodes the yellow LED arm as the
// representative condition for lipid accumulation (best
// single-colour result, Fig. 3d/f).
// Full screen requires 8 separate device runs (one per colour).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Dispense 8 culture droplets (12 uL each) from algae
// active reservoir into 8 algae culture zone electrodes, in
// series. Bussed dispensing ensures all 8 dispense in one
// electrode actuation sequence.
// Representative: single culture droplet lineage encoded here.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cultureDrop1       = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Dispense LipidTOX source droplet (~15 uL) from dye
// active reservoir onto dye dispensing bus, forming 8 label
// droplets (2 uL each) simultaneously via bussed electrodes.
// Representative: single label droplet encoded here.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

labelDrop1         = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Dispense 8 daughter culture droplets (2 uL each)
// from culture zones to L-shaped absorbance detection
// electrodes. Device placed on transparent 384-well plate;
// PHERAstar reads absorbance at 660 nm (cell density).
// Time point 1: t = 0 h (baseline before illumination).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

daughterCulture1   = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

// Absorbance measurement at t=0 (cell density baseline).
// Device positioned on transparent 384-well plate,
// PHERAstar plate reader, 660 nm, scan matrix 15x15,
// scan width 3 mm, focal height 8.7 mm.
absorbT0_colour    = detect absorbanceDetection on daughterCulture1 for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Mix 8 daughter culture droplets with 8 label droplets
// (one-to-one merge); incubate 5 min for LipidTOX staining.
// Device placed on black 384-well plate; PHERAstar reads
// fluorescence at 488 nm ex / 520 nm em (LipidTOX/neutral lipid).
// Time point 1: t = 0 h (lipid baseline before illumination).
// After measurement, mixed droplets are driven to waste
// reservoirs; fluid wicks through 1 mm through-holes.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

stainedDrop1       = mix daughterCulture1 with labelDrop1 for 5m
fluorT0_colour     = detect lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection on stainedDrop1 for 30s

dispose stainedDrop1

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ILLUMINATION PHASE 1 (6 h, yellow LEDs, 250 umol/m2/s):
// Device placed under custom LED array (Fig. S2 in paper).
// Yellow LED array: peak ~580 nm.
// `heat` abstracts LED array incubation at ambient temp (20 C).
// After 6 h: repeat Steps 4-5 for time point 2 measurement.
// 6 h = 360m
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat cultureDrop1 at 20c for 360m

// Time point 2 absorbance (t = 6 h).
daughterCulture2   = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica
absorbT6_colour    = detect absorbanceDetection on daughterCulture2 for 30s

labelDrop2         = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock
stainedDrop2       = mix daughterCulture2 with labelDrop2 for 5m
fluorT6_colour     = detect lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection on stainedDrop2 for 30s

dispose stainedDrop2

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ILLUMINATION PHASE 2 (remaining 18 h, yellow LEDs):
// Device incubated a further 18 h under yellow illumination
// to complete the 24 h total exposure.
// After 24 h total: repeat Steps 4-5 for time point 3.
// 18 h = 1080m
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat cultureDrop1 at 20c for 1080m

// Time point 3 absorbance (t = 24 h, primary endpoint).
daughterCulture3   = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

// QC gate keyed on absorbance signal at t=24h.
absorbSignal1      = detect absorbanceDetection on daughterCulture3 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Multicolour screen QC gate (absorbance at 24 h)
// Pass (BB2): absorbSignal1 > 0 -> valid cell density; proceed
//             to fluorescence measurement and lipid quantitation.
// Fail (BB3): absorbSignal1 <= 0 -> no cells (settling/dropout);
//             drain culture droplet.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (colourJoin).
// ============================================================

if (absorbSignal1 > 0) {
    labelDrop3         = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock
    stainedDrop3       = mix daughterCulture3 with labelDrop3 for 5m
    fluorT24_colour    = detect lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection on stainedDrop3 for 30s
    dispose stainedDrop3
    dispose fluorT24_colour
} else {
    drain daughterCulture3
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: colourJoin
// Dispose multicolour screen QC signals. Control falls into
// blue/yellow cycling screen (Protocol 2).
// ============================================================

dispose absorbSignal1
dispose absorbT0_colour
dispose fluorT0_colour
dispose absorbT6_colour
dispose fluorT6_colour

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 2: BLUE/YELLOW CYCLING SCREEN
// Optimal condition: 15 h blue (450 nm) / 9 h yellow (580 nm).
// High intensity: 250 umol/m2/s throughout.
// This condition produced ~4x lipid increase vs. control
// (Fig. 4b) and scaled to macroscale (200 mL flasks, Fig. 4d).
// Other 7 timing variants follow the same structure.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Fresh culture droplet for the blue/yellow cycling run.
// Active reservoir re-circulates to maintain homogeneity
// before dispensing for Protocol 2.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cultureDrop_BY     = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

// Baseline measurement before cycling illumination (t = 0 h).
labelDrop_BY0      = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock
daughter_BY0       = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

absorbBY_T0        = detect absorbanceDetection on daughter_BY0 for 30s

stained_BY0        = mix daughter_BY0 with labelDrop_BY0 for 5m
fluorBY_T0         = detect lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection on stained_BY0 for 30s

dispose stained_BY0

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// BLUE PHASE (15 h, LED array ~450 nm, 250 umol/m2/s):
// Blue illumination supports high algal growth rate
// (highest biomass accumulation, consistent with chlorophyll c
// absorbance maxima at blue wavelengths).
// 15 h = 900m
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat cultureDrop_BY at 20c for 900m

// Mid-point measurement after 15 h blue (t = 15 h).
daughter_BY15      = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica
labelDrop_BY15     = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock

absorbBY_T15       = detect absorbanceDetection on daughter_BY15 for 30s

stained_BY15       = mix daughter_BY15 with labelDrop_BY15 for 5m
fluorBY_T15        = detect lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection on stained_BY15 for 30s

dispose stained_BY15

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// YELLOW PHASE (9 h, LED array ~580 nm, 250 umol/m2/s):
// Yellow phase drives neutral lipid accumulation via
// photooxidative stress while maintaining growth rates
// established during the preceding blue phase.
// 9 h = 540m
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat cultureDrop_BY at 20c for 540m

// Final measurement after 9 h yellow / 24 h total (t = 24 h).
daughter_BY24      = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

// QC gate keyed on absorbance at t=24h.
absorbSignal2      = detect absorbanceDetection on daughter_BY24 for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Blue/yellow screen QC gate (absorbance at 24 h)
// Pass (BB5): absorbSignal2 > 0 -> valid cell density; proceed
//             to lipid fluorescence measurement at t=24h.
// Fail (BB6): absorbSignal2 <= 0 -> no cells; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (blueYellowJoin).
// ============================================================

if (absorbSignal2 > 0) {
    labelDrop_BY24     = dispense 1 units of LipidTOX_Stock
    stained_BY24       = mix daughter_BY24 with labelDrop_BY24 for 5m
    fluorBY_T24        = detect lipidTOXFluorescenceDetection on stained_BY24 for 30s
    dispose stained_BY24
    dispose fluorBY_T24
} else {
    drain daughter_BY24
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: blueYellowJoin
// Dispose blue/yellow screen QC signals. Control falls into
// ROS mechanistic assay (Protocol 3).
// ============================================================

dispose absorbSignal2
dispose absorbBY_T0
dispose fluorBY_T0
dispose absorbBY_T15
dispose fluorBY_T15

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 3: ROS MECHANISTIC ASSAY (DCFDA)
// Tests whether yellow illumination increases reactive oxygen
// species (ROS) production relative to blue and normal
// (12 h white/12 h dark) conditions, and whether ascorbate
// antioxidant reverses the effect (Fig. 5c).
//
// Conditions encoded (three sequential arms):
//   Arm A: Yellow 24 h (ROS positive)
//   Arm B: Blue 24 h (ROS negative control)
//   Arm C: Yellow 24 h + ascorbate (antioxidant rescue)
//   Arm D: Silicon deprivation (positive control, off-chip)
//     -- omitted here as it is an off-chip macroscale control
//        run in 200 mL Pyrex flasks, not on the DMF device.
//
// DCFDA PROTOCOL (macroscale, abstracted on-chip):
//   Algae grown at 5e6 cells/mL in 200 mL Pyrex flasks under
//   standard conditions (12 h light/dark) for >=1.5 weeks.
//   Cells centrifuged (3000 rpm, 5 min), resuspended in 50 mL
//   complete media or complete media without sodium silicate
//   or complete media + 50 ug/mL ascorbic acid.
//   Illuminated under assigned condition.
//   DCFDA kit: cells incubated at 37 C for 30 min in dark,
//   washed 1x, re-suspended; 150 uL aliquots read in
//   black-bottom 96-well plates.
//   `heat` at 37 C for 30 min abstracts DCFDA incubation.
//   `detect rosFluorescenceDetection` abstracts CLARIOStar/
//   PHERAstar readout (ex 490 nm / em 526 nm for DCFDA/MUF).
//
// NOTE: ROS assay was validated at macroscale (200 mL flasks);
// BioScript encodes the on-chip abstraction for consistency
// with the DMF screening context of the paper.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM A: YELLOW 24 h -- ROS positive arm
// Fresh algae in complete media, illuminated yellow 24 h.
// 24 h = 1440m (illumination); DCFDA incubation: 30m at 37C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rosAlgae_Yellow    = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

// Yellow illumination (24 h = 1440m).
heat rosAlgae_Yellow at 20c for 1440m

// DCFDA staining incubation (37 C, 30 min, dark).
heat rosAlgae_Yellow at 37c for 30m

// Fluorescence detection: DCFDA ROS reporter (ex 490 / em 526).
// QC gate keyed on yellow arm (highest expected ROS signal).
rosSignalYellow    = detect rosFluorescenceDetection on rosAlgae_Yellow for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM B: BLUE 24 h -- ROS negative control
// Fresh algae in complete media, illuminated blue 24 h.
// Blue light supports high growth (chlorophyll c maxima)
// but does not drive photooxidative stress; expected low ROS.
// 24 h = 1440m
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rosAlgae_Blue      = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica

heat rosAlgae_Blue at 20c for 1440m
heat rosAlgae_Blue at 37c for 30m

rosSignalBlue      = detect rosFluorescenceDetection on rosAlgae_Blue for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ARM C: YELLOW 24 h + ASCORBATE -- antioxidant rescue
// Complete media supplemented with 50 ug/mL ascorbic acid.
// Ascorbate scavenges ROS; reversal of yellow-light ROS
// elevation confirms photooxidative stress mechanism (Fig. 5c).
// 24 h = 1440m
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rosAlgae_Ascorbate = dispense 1 units of CyclotellaCryptica
ascorbateDrop      = dispense 1 units of AscorbicAcid

rosAlgae_AscMix    = mix rosAlgae_Ascorbate with ascorbateDrop for 5s

heat rosAlgae_AscMix at 20c for 1440m
heat rosAlgae_AscMix at 37c for 30m

rosSignalAscorbate = detect rosFluorescenceDetection on rosAlgae_AscMix for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: ROS assay QC gate (keyed on yellow arm)
// Pass (BB8): rosSignalYellow > 0 -> valid DCFDA fluorescence
//             detected; dispose all three ROS arm droplets.
//             Expected: Yellow > Blue; Yellow+Ascorbate ~ Blue
//             (antioxidant rescue confirmed).
// Fail (BB9): rosSignalYellow <= 0 -> no ROS signal
//             (DCFDA failure or cell dropout); drain all.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (rosSignalYellow > 0) {
    dispose rosAlgae_Yellow
    dispose rosAlgae_Blue
    dispose rosAlgae_AscMix
} else {
    drain rosAlgae_Yellow
    drain rosAlgae_Blue
    drain rosAlgae_AscMix
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all ROS assay QC signal droplets.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose rosSignalYellow
dispose rosSignalBlue
dispose rosSignalAscorbate

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
